# Mirror the web platform

This Expo/Android app is a mobile counterpart of the web English Journal app. **Feature behavior, UX flows, data model, and product rules must stay consistent with the web source.** Do not invent divergent product behavior.

## Canonical source

Web repo (sibling directory):

`/home/dangtran/Development/Learning/learn-english-journaling`

Primary code lives under:

- `src/app/` — routes / screens
- `src/components/` — UI
- `src/hooks/` — client logic
- `src/lib/` — API, Supabase, AI, helpers
- `src/types/` — shared types
- `supabase/` — schema and storage

## Before implementing any feature or non-trivial fix

1. Locate the matching web implementation (component, hook, lib, route, or schema).
2. Read how it works end-to-end: user flow, state, persistence, edge cases, and copy.
3. Port the same behavior to this app, adapting only for React Native / Expo constraints (navigation, gestures, native modules, layout).
4. Prefer matching naming, domain concepts, and data shapes from the web app when practical.

## Platform adaptations (allowed)

- Use Expo / React Native APIs instead of web-only APIs (DOM, Next.js server actions, browser storage, etc.).
- Adjust layout and chrome for mobile (safe areas, sheets, native keyboards) without changing the product rules.
- If a web pattern cannot work on native, implement the closest equivalent and note the intentional difference briefly in the PR/commit description.

## Do not

- Skip reading the web source and “guess” how a feature should work.
- Change product rules (save cadence, review flows, auth, preferences, entry structure) to differ from web without an explicit user request.
- Treat this repo’s incomplete or older mobile code as more authoritative than the web implementation when they conflict—**web wins** unless the user says otherwise.
